From: limina <gustavo@noronha.eti.br>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: accept XBGR8888/ABGR8888 on the primary plane (limina direct scanout)

The primary plane accepts only the XRGB/ARGB byte order, so RGBA-order
buffers can never be scanned out directly: Vulkan clients' swapchains are
typically VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_* (DRM XBGR8888/ABGR8888), and a Vulkan-
rendering compositor that wants to render straight into its scanout buffer
in that order is forced into a shadow pass + a swizzling present blit on
every frame instead.

virtio-gpu already has the format vocabulary for this
(VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_R8G8B8X8_UNORM / R8G8B8A8_UNORM); the driver just never
mapped the DRM side. Add XBGR8888/ABGR8888 to the primary-plane format
list and their translations. The limina host displays RGBA-order
IOSurfaces natively (verified against WindowServer,
spikes/scanout-modifiers/), and its venus scanout path already maps
VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_* to RGBA IOSurfaces.

Note: plain (non-HOST_) fourccs — drm_fourcc.h has no HOST_XBGR8888
byte-swap alias, and every limina guest is little-endian. A big-endian
guest would need the same treatment XRGB gets; flag if this ever goes to
dri-devel (together with the device-advertised-format-list idea, which
would make hardcoding formats here unnecessary altogether).

Two-tier note: limina enhanced-tier kernel; a stock kernel keeps the
XRGB-only plane (composited/swizzled path, correct, just more guest GPU
work). Applies on top of 0002 (ARGB8888 on the primary plane).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -37,4 +37,6 @@
 static const uint32_t virtio_gpu_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_XRGB8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_ARGB8888,
+	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888,
+	DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888,
 };
@@ -60,6 +62,12 @@
 	case DRM_FORMAT_BGRA8888:
 		format = VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_A8R8G8B8_UNORM;
 		break;
+	case DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888:
+		format = VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_R8G8B8X8_UNORM;
+		break;
+	case DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888:
+		format = VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM;
+		break;
 	default:
 		/*
 		 * This should not happen, we handle everything listed
